# Screen chrome spacing

Three families — do not merge their geometry:

| Family | Shell | Mid-list errors | Cold empty |
|---|---|---|---|
| Glass lists | `OsAppScreen` + compact/glass | `OsChromeListAlert` | `ListLoadError` |
| Immersive | Guild / hero (`immersiveHeader`) | Rail-aware overlay | In-flow state card |
| Sheets / forms | Gesture / glass sheets | Whisper only if shoving painted rows | In-flow hint |

## Shared

- Measure permanent chrome (`--os-screen-chrome-height`); tuck is visual-only (freeze inset).
- Under-chrome overlays: `.os-chrome-whisper-anchor` — never reserve flow when hidden.
- Messages sealed-thread hint: `OsChromeWhisper` (do not in-flow shove bubbles). Passkey hint stays overlay and hides on the thread pane.
- Body inset: `OsAppChromePage` / `--os-screen-body-inset` — no feature-level padding inventing numbers. Pages and sheets use `--os-gutter` (0.5rem). `--os-screen-body-pad-x` and `--os-sheet-pad-inline` both derive from it. Safe-area gutters use `max(var(--os-gutter|sheet-pad), env(safe-area-inset-*))`. Full-bleed chrome that cancels the inset (`margin: 0 calc(-1 * …)`) must use the same token on the matching padding — never a bare length.
- Dock control box: `--os-dock-height` / `--os-icon-hit` / `--os-control-primary` are one ladder at `3.25rem` on all viewports. Bottom offset stays `0.9rem`. `--portfolio-dock-clearance` derives from dock height, `--os-dock-bottom-offset`, `--os-dock-clearance-gap`, and the bottom safe area once. Compact heading / search band is separate: `--os-nav-band` `2.35rem` (not tied to dock hits). `--os-avatar-nav` `1.85rem` on all viewports (~1.35× dock glyphs for filled-face weight). Phone only thickens grip. Do not bump the root font size. Person/catalog rows share identity name/meta/bio + `--os-avatar-feed` (`lg`). Aside dates/catalog meta use `--os-stamp-size`; post `· time` stays on meta. Button labels: `--os-control-label-size` (md), `--os-control-label-compact-size`, `--os-control-label-sm-size` (sm pills/chips). Sheet/screen chrome titles: `--os-title-size` (`1.05rem`). Type/glyph ladder lives in `@onsocial/ui` `os-surface-interactive` — app `:root` only adds feed/layout tokens (`--os-avatar-feed`, `--os-post-body-size`, dock). Inline ⋮: `--os-menu-glyph-size` / `--os-menu-hit-size`. Engagement: `--os-engagement-glyph-size`. Chrome × / face ⋮: `--os-chrome-glyph-size` (`1.5rem`, scales with dock). Display heroes and reading/immersive prose stay above the ladder on purpose. Launcher grid tiles: `--os-launcher-icon-size` `3.6rem` + `--os-launcher-glyph-size` `1.6rem` (larger than feed `lg` avatar `2.5rem`). Labels use stamp (`--os-launcher-label-size` → `--os-stamp-size`). Launcher header rail: OnSocial mark + name stay the subject; Rally + × share `--os-nav-band` hits with `--os-chrome-glyph-size` glyphs (Rally label `--os-control-label-compact-size`) — unlayered like `standing-sheet-header--compact` so dock `--os-icon-hit` mins do not win. `SheetChromeHeader` always adds `--compact` so boost / rally / account / Discover overlay closes share that rail. Title-centric `SheetHeader` / `.glass-sheet-header` × hits use the same nav band (unlayered); title `padding-top` tracks that hit so the first line stays optically centered. Header action glyphs (× / Back / Discover / Globe / Add) use `.glass-sheet-icon-action-glyph` → `--os-chrome-glyph-size`; search-in-field and menu ⋮ stay on their own ladder. Home Hot/Recent sort: nav-band hit + chrome glyph — not dock `--os-icon-hit`. Home full chip-rail tuck zeros body pad in CSS; search tuck still freezes `--os-screen-chrome-height`.

## Live vs cold

- Painted rows → overlay (`OsChromeListAlert`).
- Empty / first paint → in-flow (`ListLoadError`).
- Soft revalidate that keeps a cache must keep painting the cache and whisper the failure — never blank to `ListLoadError`.
